# What the build context must not carry. The context is src/agents, so everything here is
# relative to it.

# A COPY that picked this up would bake the agent_svc password and both shared secrets
# into a layer, where `docker history` reads them back out of any copy of the image.
# Secrets reach a container through the environment, never through a build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# This machine's own virtualenv: a few hundred megabytes of wheels built for this kernel,
# and the image builds its own. Copying it in would also shadow the installed package.
.venv

# Stale bytecode. This checkout still has .pyc files for app/infrastructure/ag2/team.py,
# a module deleted in stage 3 - and a .pyc without its .py is importable, so a build that
# carried them could run code that no longer exists in the repository.
__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# Not the service. The tests have their own job in CI, and `dist` is the wheel the CI
# regression guard builds - neither belongs in an image that talks to a broker.
tests
dist
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
